# This repo is worked from Windows but half of it is deployed to Linux.
# Anything that a Linux shell or systemd has to parse must keep LF endings:
# bash fails on a CRLF shebang line, and systemd silently mis-parses CRLF
# directives.
# Python here is deployed to BOTH machines and the cross-machine
# corroboration argument depends on the two copies being byte-identical.
# A CRLF checkout on Windows would silently change the sha256.
*.py            text eol=lf
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.service       text eol=lf
deploy/laptop/* text eol=lf
# Windows-side drivers stay CRLF; cmd.exe is fine either way but the files are
# edited on Windows.
*.cmd           text eol=crlf
*.vbs           text eol=crlf
